   "id": "5-systematic-circuit-analysis-nodal-vs-mesh",
   "title": "5. Systematic Circuit Analysis: Nodal vs. Mesh",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "5.1 Nodal Analysis by Inspection"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "Applicable to networks with conductances and independent current sources:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\begin{bmatrix} G_{11} & G_{12} & \\cdots & G_{1n} \\\\ G_{21} & G_{22} & \\cdots & G_{2n} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\ G_{n1} & G_{n2} & \\cdots & G_{nn} \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} V_1 \\\\ V_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ V_n \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} I_1 \\\\ I_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ I_n \\end{bmatrix}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "$G_{ii} = \\sum$ Conductances directly connected to node $i$ (strictly positive).",
      "$G_{ij} = -(\\sum \\text{Conductances connected between nodes } i \\text{ and } j)$ for $i \\neq j$ (strictly negative or zero).",
      "$I_i = \\sum$ Independent currents entering node $i$ minus currents leaving."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "5.2 Supernode Technique"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Condition**: An ideal voltage source (independent or dependent) is connected between two non-reference nodes $A$ and $B$.",
      "**Procedure**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 1,
     "items": [
      "Enclose the voltage source and its connecting terminals in a generalized Gaussian surface (supernode).",
      "Write **1 combined KCL equation** for currents leaving the supernode boundary.",
      "Write **1 auxiliary constraint equation** across the source:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "V_A - V_B = V_{\\text{source}}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "5.3 Mesh Analysis by Inspection"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "Applicable to planar networks with resistances and independent voltage sources:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\begin{bmatrix} R_{11} & R_{12} & \\cdots & R_{1m} \\\\ R_{21} & R_{22} & \\cdots & R_{2m} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\ R_{m1} & R_{m2} & \\cdots & R_{mm} \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} I_1 \\\\ I_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ I_m \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} V_1 \\\\ V_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ V_m \\end{bmatrix}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "$R_{ii} = \\sum$ Resistances around mesh $i$ (strictly positive).",
      "$R_{ij} = -(\\sum \\text{Resistances shared between meshes } i \\text{ and } j)$ for $i \\neq j$.",
      "$V_i = \\text{Net clockwise driving voltage in mesh } i$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "5.4 Supermesh Technique"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Condition**: An ideal current source is shared between two adjacent meshes 1 and 2.",
      "**Procedure**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 1,
     "items": [
      "Mentally open-circuit the current source branch, forming a larger combined loop (supermesh).",
      "Write **1 perimeter KVL equation** around the outer boundary of the supermesh.",
      "Write **1 auxiliary constraint equation** relating the two mesh currents:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "I_{\\text{mesh 2}} - I_{\\text{mesh 1}} = I_{\\text{source}}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "5.5 Graph Topology & Selection Criterion"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "For a connected planar graph with $b$ branches and $n$ nodes:",
      "Number of independent node pairs: $N_{\\text{nodal}} = n - 1$.",
      "Number of independent fundamental loops (meshes): $M = b - n + 1$.",
      "**Decision Rule**: Use Nodal if $(n - 1) < (b - n + 1)$; use Mesh if $(b - n + 1) < (n - 1)$."
     ]
    }
   ]
