   "id": "6-network-reductions-bridges-geometric-symmetry",
   "title": "6. Network Reductions, Bridges & Geometric Symmetry",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "6.1 Star-Delta ($\\text{Y} \\leftrightarrow \\Delta$) Transformations"
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "text": "           Delta (\u0394) Network                               Star (Y) Network\n                  A                                               A\n                 /\\                                               \u2502\n                /  \\                                              \u2502 R_1\n            R_B/    \\R_C                                          \u2502\n              /      \\                                            o N\n             /   R_A  \\                                          / \\\n            B\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500C                                    R_2 /   \\ R_3\n                                                               /     \\\n                                                              B       C"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{\\textbf{Delta to Star (Y)}}: \\quad & R_1 = \\frac{R_B R_C}{R_A + R_B + R_C}, \\quad R_2 = \\frac{R_C R_A}{R_A + R_B + R_C}, \\quad R_3 = \\frac{R_A R_B}{R_A + R_B + R_C} \\\\\n\\text{\\textbf{Star to Delta (}\\Delta\\text{)}}: \\quad & R_A = R_2 + R_3 + \\frac{R_2 R_3}{R_1}, \\quad R_B = R_1 + R_3 + \\frac{R_1 R_3}{R_2}, \\quad R_C = R_1 + R_2 + \\frac{R_1 R_2}{R_3}\n\\end{aligned}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Symmetric Identical Branches**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "R_\\Delta = 3 R_Y \\iff R_Y = \\frac{R_\\Delta}{3}, \\qquad L_\\Delta = 3 L_Y \\iff L_Y = \\frac{L_\\Delta}{3}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Capacitor Duality Inversion** ($Y_C = j\\omega C \\propto C$):"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\mathbf{C_\\Delta = \\frac{C_Y}{3} \\iff C_Y = 3 C_\\Delta}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "6.2 Wheatstone Bridge"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Balanced Condition**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\frac{R_1}{R_2} = \\frac{R_3}{R_4} \\iff R_1 R_4 = R_2 R_3"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "When balanced: $V_{\\text{detector}} = 0\\text{ V}, I_{\\text{detector}} = 0\\text{ A}$. The central detector arm can be **either OPENED or SHORTED** without changing input resistance."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "6.3 Geometric Symmetry & 3D Cube Resistance Mnemonic"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "For a cube consisting of 12 identical resistors of value $R$:"
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "text": "   12-Resistor Cube Orientations:\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 Across Edge (Adjacent vertices A-B):     R_edge = (7/12) R  \u2248 0.583 R\n   \u251c\u2500\u2500 Across Face Diagonal (Vertices A-C):     R_face = (9/12) R  = 0.750 R\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500 Across Body Diagonal (Opposite A-H):     R_body = (10/12) R \u2248 0.833 R"
    },
    {
     "t": "alert",
     "type": "TIP",
     "title": null,
     "text": "**Faculty Speed Mnemonic for 12-Resistor Cube**:\nGroup the fractions by denominator 12 in strictly ascending order:\n$$\\mathbf{\\frac{7}{12}R \\;<\\; \\frac{9}{12}R \\;<\\; \\frac{10}{12}R} \\quad \\iff \\quad \\mathbf{\\text{Edge} \\;<\\; \\text{Face} \\;<\\; \\text{Body}}$$"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Hexagonal Spoke Wheel (12 resistors $R$)**: Across center hub and any rim node:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "R_{\\text{eq}} = \\frac{4}{5}R = 0.8R"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Infinite 2D Square Grid of Resistors $R$**:",
      "Across two immediately adjacent nodes: $R_{\\text{adj}} = \\frac{R}{2} = 0.5R$ (by 4-fold superposition).",
      "Across two diagonal nodes: $R_{\\text{diag}} = \\frac{2}{3}R \\approx 0.667R$.",
      "**Infinite Periodic Ladder Network**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "R_{\\text{in}} = R_1 + (R_2 \\parallel R_{\\text{in}}) \\implies R_{\\text{in}}^2 - R_1 R_{\\text{in}} - R_1 R_2 = 0"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "For $R_1 = 1\\,\\Omega, R_2 = 2\\,\\Omega$: $R_{\\text{in}} = 1 + \\frac{2 R_{\\text{in}}}{2 + R_{\\text{in}}} \\implies R_{\\text{in}} = \\mathbf{2\\,\\Omega}$."
    }
   ]
